@page "/privacy"
<PageTitle>Privacy and test limits — Retry Assurance</PageTitle><h1>Privacy and test limits</h1>
<section class="panel"><h2>Use test data</h2><p>Your code runs on your computer or in your build. The supplied transport sends requests only to the issued test endpoint and replaces credentials with dummy values.</p><p>It does not remove sensitive values from a request body or stop code that uses a separate connection. Do not send production keys, personal data or customer requests.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What is stored</h2><p>We store account and access records, project settings, client/build labels, request order, body sizes and fingerprints, test-job IDs, results and the client note you submit.</p><p>Raw request bodies and arbitrary headers are not retained. Recovery keys and runner keys are stored as hashes. Do not put secrets in names, labels or client notes. The operator can access stored service data.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What a result means</h2><p>A result checks recorded job creation in the selected scenario. Client names, build labels and final outcomes are supplied by the runner, not independently verified source code.</p><p>Recorded reply statuses describe the test endpoint's prepared response. They do not prove the client received it. Exported local timing observations and the request journal measure different parts of the check.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Access and deletion</h2><p>Owners manage settings and members. Editors run checks; viewers read results. Revoking a runner key or removing its editor stops further access through that key. Authorized members can still read saved results.</p><p>Each run must finish within thirty minutes. Export anything you need before deleting your account and owned data on the <a href="/account">account page</a>. An active paid period must end first. Exported copies are not recalled by deletion.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Payment and preferences</h2><p>When checkout is available, Stripe handles card and subscription details. The service stores its linked subscription status and period; it does not collect card numbers.</p><p>This site saves the theme preference on your device. It loads no advertising trackers or analytics. Logs exclude submitted request bodies and credential values.</p></section>
